[1m[38;5;10mrpl_asprintf[0m[22m: The original implementation used [38;5;10msize=0[0m for a first pass to determine length, then a second pass to write. This didn't work because the Rust format functions ([38;5;10mfmtstr[0m, [38;5;10mfmtint[0m, [38;5;10mfmtflt[0m) track length via [38;5;10ms.len()[0m internally — when [38;5;10msize=0[0m, nothing gets written to [38;5;10ms[0m, so [38;5;10ms.len()[0m stays 0 and the returned length is wrong. Fixed by using [38;5;10musize::MAX[0m as size so content is always written in a single pass.[0m[0m[38;5;12m[1m✓ Created checkpoint 1

